{
  "language_code": "eng",
  "language_probability": 1.0,
  "text": "Thermal telemetry online. Four thousand Kelvin at the source. We have reached the foundry forge. Those conduits feed the Citadel sky shields. Shut this reactor down and their fortress loses its cover. Forced labor built this place. Heavy coils, thick walls. They planned for a meltdown. They did not plan for us. Three aquifers drained to cool their turbines. Break the valves and the river can take its course again. That turbine is deafening, but beneath the grind, I can hear a fault in the containment lattice. Turrets on the catwalks. Slag below. I have a road over the coolant lines. Watch your footing. My bulwark will cover the radiation crossing. Once we breach the core, we move straight to extraction. When that reactor goes, their shield goes with it. Let us see how brave they are without it. Sever the coolant lines. Overload the reactor. Break their sky shields. Axiom force, drop in.",
